{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f3a2b1c-4d5e-4f6a-8b9c-0d1e2f3a4b5c",
    "name": "Bookmark API",
    "description": "# Bookmark API\n\nOfficial API Collection for the **Bookmark** platform.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture & Endpoints Overview\n\n| Service | Base Route | Key Features |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Auth Service** | `/auth` | Signup, Login, Refresh Token, Logout |\n| **User Service** | `/user` | Get Profile, Update Profile |\n| **Bookmark Service** | `/bookmark` | Create, List, Get by ID, Update, Delete |\n\n---\n\n## Dynamic Environment Variables\n- `baseUrl`: `http://localhost:3000` (NestJS server URL)\n- `token`: Bearer access token (saved by Sign Up / Login / Refresh Token)\n- `refreshToken`: JWT refresh token (sent as Bearer on Refresh Token; rotated on every refresh)\n- `userId`: Authenticated user ID\n- `userEmail`: User email (auto-generated per run)\n- `bookmarkId`: Created/selected bookmark ID\n- `bookmarkTitle`: Created bookmark title\n- `updateTitle`: Updated bookmark title\n\n---\n\n## Run Order\n\nRun the collection top-to-bottom. A unique email is generated on every Sign Up, so the whole collection is re-runnable without duplicate key errors. **Logout intentionally runs last**: it revokes the server-side tokens (deletes the stored refresh token and blacklists the access token), so every request that needs a valid token must run before it. The flow: **Sign Up → Login → Refresh Token → Get Profile → Update Profile → Create Bookmark → Get Bookmarks → Get Bookmark by ID → Update Bookmark → Delete Bookmark → Logout**.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57587615"
  },
  "item": [
